      "writtenOn": "2020-12-17T20:38:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\"no_standard_libs: true\" aka \"sdk_version: \"none\"\" removes a lot more than the framework.jar APIs, it also removes all the libcore APIs.  Very little should actually need that.  Most places will want \"no_framework_libs: true\", which is now known as \"sdk_version: \"core_current\"\".\n\nIIRC, my worry was that people would use \"sdk_version: \"none\", libs: [\"core-oj\", \"core-libart\", ...]\" when they should be using \"sdk_version: \"core_current\"\".  Then adding a new jar to the core APIs requires finding everywhere someone has done this incorrectly and updating them.\n\nIf that\u0027s not something you\u0027re worried about I\u0027m fine with removing this.",
      "parentUuid": "eaa1346e_f9642f45",
      "revId": "0af20effc1d52bce16c40b04e6e9a5881e03c65e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
